* Selectable-Clip Overdrive — exported from Lutherie
* An op-amp overdrive with a three-way Clip selector in its feedback loop. A: two back-to-back MOSFETs, which clip late and softly (open, amp-like). B: two silicon diodes, which clip early (compressed, more driven). Centre: no clipping parts, a clean boost until the op-amp itself runs out of swing.

Vsig SIGSRC 0 SIN(0 0.3 220.0) AC 1
Rsig SIGSRC IN 1k
CC1 IN N2 47n
RR1 N2 N3 10k
RR2 N3 VCC_4p5V 1Meg
XU1 N3 N5 N6 OPAMP_TL072_15_75
RR3 N5 N6 220k
RR4 N7 N5 4.7k
CC2 N8 N7 100n
* Drive pot 100k B taper at 70%
RVR1a 0 0 70k
RVR1b 0 N8 30k
MM1 N5 N5 N9 N9 M_BS170
CM1gs N5 N9 24p
CM1gd N5 N5 7p
MM2 N10 N10 N9 N9 M_BS170
CM2gs N10 N9 24p
CM2gd N10 N10 7p
DD1 N5 N11 D_1N4148
DD2 N11 N5 D_1N4148
RSW1 N6 N10 0.05
CC3 N6 N12 1u
RR5 N12 N13 1k
CC4 N13 0 22n
* Level pot 100k A taper at 70%
RVR2a 0 OUT 25.8k
RVR2b OUT N13 74.2k
Rload OUT 0 1Meg
VVS1 VCC_4p5V_src 0 DC 4.5
RVS1s VCC_4p5V_src VCC_4p5V 0.01

.model D_1N4148 D(Is=2.52e-09 N=1.752 Rs=0.568 Cjo=4e-12 M=0)
.model M_BS170 NMOS(Level=1 Vto=1.9 Kp=0.08 Lambda=0.0003 Is=1e-13)
* Behavioural op-amp: gain, gain-bandwidth, slew rate and output swing
.subckt OPAMP_TL072_15_75 INP INN OUT
Bin 0 M I=0.13793428401297597*tanh(0.2*V(INP,INN)/0.13793428401297597)
R1 M 0 1Meg
C1 M 0 1.061032953945969e-08
* keeps the internal node inside the swing, so the amplifier recovers from clipping at once
Bcl M 0 I=(ln(1+exp(min(6.666666666666667*(V(M)-7.5),60)))-ln(1+exp(min(6.666666666666667*(-V(M)-7.5),60))))/6.666666666666667
* soft saturation x/(1+x^4)^(1/4), written without pwr() because simulators disagree on its sign
Bout X 0 V=4.5+V(M)/sqrt(sqrt(1+(V(M)/3.0)*(V(M)/3.0)*(V(M)/3.0)*(V(M)/3.0)))
Rout X OUT 75.0
.ends

.options reltol=1e-5 abstol=1e-13 vntol=1e-8 method=trap
.tran 1.3020833333333333e-06 0.3 0 1.3020833333333333e-06
.control
set wr_singlescale
set numdgt=12
run
wrdata selectable_clip_overdrive.ngspice.txt v(OUT)
.endc
.end